#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mid-circuit measurements {#mid-circuit-measurements}"
msgstr "Mga mid-circuit measurement {#mid-circuit-measurements}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Prior to `qiskit-ibm-runtime` v0.43.0, `measure` was the only measurement instruction in Qiskit. Mid-circuit measurements, however, have different tuning requirements than _terminal_ measurements (measurements that happen at the end of a circuit). For example, you need to consider the instruction duration when tuning a mid-circuit measurement because longer instructions cause noisier circuits. You don't need to consider instruction duration for terminal measurements because there are no instructions after terminal measurements.\n"
msgstr "Bago ang `qiskit-ibm-runtime` v0.43.0, ang `measure` ang nag-iisang tagubilin sa sukat sa Qiskit. Ang mga mid-circuit measurement, gayunpaman, ay may iba't ibang mga kinakailangan sa tuning kaysa sa mga _terminal_ measurement (mga sukat na nagaganap sa dulo ng isang circuit). Halimbawa, kailangan mong isaalang-alang ang tagal ng tagubilin kapag ino-tune ang isang mid-circuit measurement dahil ang mas matagal na mga tagubilin ay nagdudulot ng mas maingay na mga circuit. Hindi mo kailangang isaalang-alang ang tagal ng tagubilin para sa mga terminal measurement dahil walang mga tagubilin pagkatapos ng mga terminal measurement.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"The `MidCircuitMeasure` instruction maps to the `measure_2` instruction reported in the backend's `supported_instructions`. However,  `measure_2` is not supported on all backends. Use `service.backends(filters=lambda b: \"measure_2\" in b.supported_instructions)` to find backends that support it.  New measurements might be added in the future, but this is not guarenteed.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Ang tagubilin na `MidCircuitMeasure` ay nagma-map sa tagubilin na `measure_2` na iniulat sa `supported_instructions` ng backend. Gayunpaman, ang `measure_2` ay hindi sinusuportahan sa lahat ng backend. Gamitin ang `service.backends(filters=lambda b: \"measure_2\" in b.supported_instructions)` para mahanap ang mga backend na sumusuporta nito. Maaaring magdagdag ng mga bagong sukat sa hinaharap, ngunit hindi ito ginagarantiyahan.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "`MidCircuitMeasure` method {#midcircuitmeasure-method}"
msgstr "Method na `MidCircuitMeasure` {#midcircuitmeasure-method}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In `qiskit-ibm-runtime` v0.43.0, the `MidCircuitMeasure` instruction was introduced. As the name suggests, it is a new measurement instruction that is optimized for mid-circuit on IBM&reg; QPUs.  While you can use `QuantumCircuit.measure` for a mid-circuit measurement, because of its design, `MidCircuitMeasure` is typically a better choice.  For example, it adds less overhead to your circuit than when using `QuantumCircuit.measure`.\n"
msgstr "Sa `qiskit-ibm-runtime` v0.43.0, ang tagubilin na `MidCircuitMeasure` ay ipinakilala. Tulad ng iminumungkahi ng pangalan, ito ay isang bagong tagubilin sa sukat na optimized para sa mid-circuit sa IBM&reg; QPU. Habang maaari kang gumamit ng `QuantumCircuit.measure` para sa isang mid-circuit measurement, dahil sa disenyo nito, ang `MidCircuitMeasure` ay karaniwang mas magandang pagpipilian. Halimbawa, nagdaragdag ito ng mas kaunting overhead sa iyong circuit kaysa kapag gumagamit ng `QuantumCircuit.measure`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<Admonition type=\"warning\" title=\"Important notes\">\n"
msgstr "<Admonition type=\"warning\" title=\"Mahahalagang tala\">\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "There must be at least one classical register in order to use measurements.\n"
msgstr "Dapat mayroong kahit isang classical register para magamit ang mga sukat.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Sampler primitive requires circuit measurements. You can add circuit measurements with the Estimator primitive, but they are ignored.\n"
msgstr "Ang Sampler primitive ay nangangailangan ng mga sukat ng circuit. Maaari kang magdagdag ng mga sukat ng circuit sa Estimator primitive, ngunit binabalewala ang mga ito.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "`Store` {#store}"
msgstr "`Store` {#store}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With `qiskit-ibm-runtime` version 0.47.0 or later, you can use the [`store`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/circuit#store) instruction to save the result of a classical expression, if that expression will be used repeatedly. Operations are automatically parallelized, making your code significantly more efficient at runtime.\n"
msgstr "Sa `qiskit-ibm-runtime` bersyon 0.47.0 o mas bago, maaari mong gamitin ang tagubilin na [`store`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/circuit#store) para i-save ang resulta ng isang classical expression, kung ang expression na iyon ay gagamitin nang paulit-ulit. Ang mga operasyon ay awtomatikong pinara-parallel, na ginagawang mas mahusay ang iyong code sa runtime.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For more information, see the [Classical feedforward and control flow](/guides/classical-feedforward-and-control-flow#store) guide.\n"
msgstr "Para sa karagdagang impormasyon, tingnan ang gabay na [Classical feedforward and control flow](/guides/classical-feedforward-and-control-flow#store).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<DoqAdmonition type=\"note\">\n"
msgstr "<DoqAdmonition type=\"note\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When you use `store` to save a value to a classical register on a real backend, that value is only saved in memory during execution and not copied or returned in the job result.\n"
msgstr "Kapag ginamit mo ang `store` para i-save ang isang value sa isang classical register sa isang tunay na backend, ang value na iyon ay naka-save lamang sa memory sa panahon ng execution at hindi kinokopya o ibinalik sa resulta ng job.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For example, in the following code, `temp` has the same value as `creg` during execution, and the `if_test` works as expected. But after the job finishes, the `temp` BitArray returned in the job result **does not** contain the value of `creg`.  That is, `job.result()[0].data.temp` is `0`.\n"
msgstr "Halimbawa, sa sumusunod na code, ang `temp` ay may parehong value ng `creg` sa panahon ng execution, at gumagana ang `if_test` ayon sa inaasahan. Ngunit pagkatapos matapos ang job, ang `temp` BitArray na ibinalik sa resulta ng job **ay hindi** naglalaman ng value ng `creg`. Ibig sabihin, ang `job.result()[0].data.temp` ay `0`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "</DoqAdmonition>\n"
msgstr "</DoqAdmonition>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Full example {#full-example}"
msgstr "Kumpletong halimbawa {#full-example}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following code creates and runs a dynamic circuit on IBM&reg; hardware.\n"
msgstr "Ang sumusunod na code ay lumilikha at nagpapatakbo ng isang dynamic na circuit sa IBM&reg; hardware.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Qiskit Runtime limitations {#qiskit-runtime-limitations}"
msgid "Quantum Compute limitations {#quantum-compute-limitations}"
msgstr "Mga limitasyon ng Qiskit Runtime {#qiskit-runtime-limitations}"

#. type: Plain text
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Be aware of the following constraints when running dynamic circuits in Qiskit Runtime.\n"
msgid "Be aware of the following constraints when running dynamic circuits in Quantum Compute.\n"
msgstr "Maging aware ng mga sumusunod na limitasyon kapag nagpapatakbo ng mga dynamic na circuit sa Qiskit Runtime.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Due to the limited physical memory on control electronics, there is also a limit on the number of `if` statements and size of their operands. This limit is a function of the number of broadcasts and the number of broadcasted bits in a job (not a circuit).\n"
msgstr "Dahil sa limitadong pisikal na memory sa mga control electronics, mayroon ding limitasyon sa bilang ng mga pahayag na `if` at laki ng kanilang mga operand. Ang limitasyong ito ay isang function ng bilang ng mga broadcast at bilang ng mga broadcasted na bit sa isang job (hindi isang circuit).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   When processing an `if` condition, measurement data needs to be transferred to the control logic to make that evaluation. A broadcast is a transfer of unique classical data, and broadcasted bits is the number of classical bits being transferred. Consider the following:\n"
msgstr "   Kapag nagpoproseso ng isang kondisyon na `if`, ang data ng sukat ay kailangang ilipat sa control logic para gawin ang pagtatasa na iyon. Ang isang broadcast ay isang paglipat ng natatanging classical data, at ang mga broadcasted na bit ay ang bilang ng mga classical bit na inililipat. Isaalang-alang ang sumusunod:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   In the previous code example, the first two `if_test` objects on `c0` are considered one broadcast because the content of `c0` did not change, and thus does not need to be re-broadcasted. The `if_test` on `c1` is a second broadcast. The first one broadcasts all three bits in `c0` and the second broadcasts just one bit, making a total of four broadcasted bits.\n"
msgstr "   Sa nakaraang halimbawa ng code, ang unang dalawang object na `if_test` sa `c0` ay itinuturing na isang broadcast dahil ang nilalaman ng `c0` ay hindi nagbago, at samakatuwid ay hindi na kailangang i-re-broadcast. Ang `if_test` sa `c1` ay isang pangalawang broadcast. Ang una ay nagba-broadcast ng lahat ng tatlong bit sa `c0` at ang pangalawa ay nagba-broadcast ng isang bit lamang, na gumagawa ng kabuuang apat na broadcasted na bit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   Currently, if you broadcast 60 bits each time, then the job can have approximately 300 broadcasts. If you broadcast just one bit each time, however, then the job can have 2400 broadcasts.\n"
msgstr "   Kasalukuyan, kung nagba-broadcast ka ng 60 bit bawat beses, ang job ay maaaring magkaroon ng humigit-kumulang 300 broadcast. Kung nagba-broadcast ka ng isang bit lamang bawat beses, gayunpaman, ang job ay maaaring magkaroon ng 2400 broadcast.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The operand used in an `if_test` statement must be 32 or fewer bits. Thus, if you are comparing an entire `ClassicalRegister`, the size of that `ClassicalRegister` must be 32 or fewer bits. If you are comparing just a single bit from a `ClassicalRegister`, however, that `ClassicalRegister` can be of any size (since the operand is only one bit).\n"
msgstr "Ang operand na ginamit sa isang pahayag na `if_test` ay dapat na 32 o mas kaunting bit. Kaya, kung ikukumpara mo ang isang buong `ClassicalRegister`, ang laki ng `ClassicalRegister` na iyon ay dapat na 32 o mas kaunting bit. Kung ikukumpara mo lamang ang isang solong bit mula sa isang `ClassicalRegister`, gayunpaman, ang `ClassicalRegister` na iyon ay maaaring may anumang laki (dahil ang operand ay isang bit lamang).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   For example, the \"Not valid\" code block does not work because `cr` is more than 32 bits.  You can, however, use a classical register wider than 32 bits if you are testing only one bit, as shown in the \"Valid\" code block.\n"
msgstr "   Halimbawa, ang \"Hindi valid\" na code block ay hindi gumagana dahil ang `cr` ay higit sa 32 bit. Maaari mong gamitin ang isang classical register na mas malawak sa 32 bit, gayunpaman, kung sinusubukan mo lamang ang isang bit, tulad ng ipinapakita sa \"Valid\" na code block.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   <Tabs>\n"
"   <TabItem value=\"Not valid\" label=\"Not valid\">\n"
msgstr ""
"   <Tabs>\n"
"   <TabItem value=\"Not valid\" label=\"Hindi valid\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"      ```python\n"
"         cr = ClassicalRegister(50)\n"
"         qr = QuantumRegister(50)\n"
"         circuit = QuantumCircuit(qr, cr)\n"
"         ...\n"
"         circ.measure(qr, cr)\n"
"         with circ.if_test((cr, 15)):\n"
"            ...\n"
"      ```\n"
"   </TabItem>\n"
"   <TabItem value=\"Valid\" label=\"Valid\">\n"
msgstr ""
"      ```python\n"
"         cr = ClassicalRegister(50)\n"
"         qr = QuantumRegister(50)\n"
"         circuit = QuantumCircuit(qr, cr)\n"
"         ...\n"
"         circ.measure(qr, cr)\n"
"         with circ.if_test((cr, 15)):\n"
"            ...\n"
"      ```\n"
"   </TabItem>\n"
"   <TabItem value=\"Valid\" label=\"Valid\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"      ```python\n"
"         cr = ClassicalRegister(50)\n"
"         qr = QuantumRegister(50)\n"
"         circuit = QuantumCircuit(qr, cr)\n"
"         ...\n"
"         circ.measure(qr, cr)\n"
"         with circ.if_test((cr[5], 1)):\n"
"            ...\n"
"      ```\n"
"   </TabItem>\n"
"   </Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"      ```python\n"
"         cr = ClassicalRegister(50)\n"
"         qr = QuantumRegister(50)\n"
"         circuit = QuantumCircuit(qr, cr)\n"
"         ...\n"
"         circ.measure(qr, cr)\n"
"         with circ.if_test((cr[5], 1)):\n"
"            ...\n"
"      ```\n"
"   </TabItem>\n"
"   </Tabs>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- Nested conditionals are not allowed. For example, the following code block will not work because it has an `if_test` inside another `if_test`:\n"
"   <Tabs>\n"
"    <TabItem value=\"Not valid\" label=\"Not valid\">\n"
msgstr ""
"- Hindi pinapayagan ang mga nested conditional. Halimbawa, ang sumusunod na code block ay hindi gagana dahil mayroon itong `if_test` sa loob ng isa pang `if_test`:\n"
"   <Tabs>\n"
"    <TabItem value=\"Not valid\" label=\"Hindi valid\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        ```python\n"
"           c1 = ClassicalRegister(1, \"c1\")\n"
"           c2 = ClassicalRegister(2, \"c2\")\n"
"           ...\n"
"           with circ.if_test((c1, 1)):\n"
"            with circ.if_test(c2, 1)):\n"
"             ...\n"
"        ```\n"
"     </TabItem>\n"
"     <TabItem value=\"Valid\" label=\"Valid\">\n"
msgstr ""
"        ```python\n"
"           c1 = ClassicalRegister(1, \"c1\")\n"
"           c2 = ClassicalRegister(2, \"c2\")\n"
"           ...\n"
"           with circ.if_test((c1, 1)):\n"
"            with circ.if_test(c2, 1)):\n"
"             ...\n"
"        ```\n"
"     </TabItem>\n"
"     <TabItem value=\"Valid\" label=\"Valid\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        ```python\n"
"        cr = ClassicalRegister(2)\n"
"        ...\n"
"        with circuit.if_test((cr, 0b11)):\n"
"          ...\n"
"        ```\n"
"     </TabItem>\n"
"    </Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"        ```python\n"
"        cr = ClassicalRegister(2)\n"
"        ...\n"
"        with circuit.if_test((cr, 0b11)):\n"
"          ...\n"
"        ```\n"
"     </TabItem>\n"
"    </Tabs>\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Having `reset` or measurements inside conditionals is not supported.\n"
msgstr "Hindi sinusuportahan ang pagkakaroon ng `reset` o mga sukat sa loob ng mga conditional.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Arithmetic operations are not supported.\n"
msgstr "Hindi sinusuportahan ang mga arithmetic operation.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "See the [OpenQASM 3 feature table](/guides/qasm-feature-table) to determine which OpenQASM 3 features are supported on Qiskit and Qiskit Runtime.\n"
msgid "See the [OpenQASM 3 feature table](/guides/qasm-feature-table) to determine which OpenQASM 3 features are supported with Qiskit and Quantum Compute.\n"
msgstr "Tingnan ang [talahanayan ng feature ng OpenQASM 3](/guides/qasm-feature-table) para matukoy kung aling mga feature ng OpenQASM 3 ang sinusuportahan sa Qiskit at Qiskit Runtime.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "When OpenQASM 3 (instead of `QuantumCircuit`) is used as the input format to pass circuits to Qiskit Runtime primitives, only instructions that can be loaded into Qiskit are supported. Classical operations, for example, are not supported because they cannot be loaded into Qiskit. See [Import an OpenQASM 3 program into Qiskit](/guides/interoperate-qiskit-qasm3#import-an-openqasm-3-program-into-qiskit) for more information.\n"
msgid "When OpenQASM 3 (instead of `QuantumCircuit`) is used as the input format to pass circuits to IBM Quantum primitives, only instructions that can be loaded into Qiskit are supported. Classical operations, for example, are not supported because they cannot be loaded into Qiskit. See [Import an OpenQASM 3 program into Qiskit](/guides/interoperate-qiskit-qasm3#import-an-openqasm-3-program-into-qiskit) for more information.\n"
msgstr "Kapag ginamit ang OpenQASM 3 (sa halip na `QuantumCircuit`) bilang format ng input para mag-pass ng mga circuit sa mga primitive ng Qiskit Runtime, sinusuportahan lamang ang mga tagubilin na maaaring i-load sa Qiskit. Ang mga classical operation, halimbawa, ay hindi sinusuportahan dahil hindi sila maaaring i-load sa Qiskit. Tingnan ang [Mag-import ng OpenQASM 3 program sa Qiskit](/guides/interoperate-qiskit-qasm3#import-an-openqasm-3-program-into-qiskit) para sa karagdagang impormasyon.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `for`, `while`, and `switch` instructions are not supported.\n"
msgstr "Hindi sinusuportahan ang mga tagubilin na `for`, `while`, at `switch`.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use dynamic circuits with Estimator {#use-dynamic-circuits-with-estimator}"
msgstr "Gumamit ng mga dynamic na circuit sa Estimator {#use-dynamic-circuits-with-estimator}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Since Estimator does not support dynamic circuits, you can use [Sampler](/guides/get-started-with-sampler) and build your own measurement circuits instead.\n"
msgstr "Dahil hindi sinusuportahan ng Estimator ang mga dynamic na circuit, maaari kang gumamit ng [Sampler](/guides/get-started-with-sampler) at bumuo ng iyong sariling mga circuit ng sukat sa halip.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To replicate Estimator's behavior, follow this process:\n"
msgstr "Para tularan ang gawi ng Estimator, sundin ang prosesong ito:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid ""
#| "1. Group the terms of all observables into a partition.  This can be done by using the [`PauliList` API](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.PauliList#group_qubit_wise_commuting), for example.\n"
#| "     <Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
#| "      You can use the [`BitArray`](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/docs/en/api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.BitArray#expectation_values) primitive attribute to compute the expectation values of the provided observables.\n"
#| "     </Admonition>\n"
#| "2. Execute one basis change circuit per partition (whichever basis change needs to be done for each partition). See the Measurement bases addon utility [`measurement_bases` module](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-utils/apidocs/qiskit_addon_utils.exp_vals.html#qiskit_addon_utils.exp_vals.get_measurement_bases) for more information. For more information, see the [documentation](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-utils/) for the Qiskit addon utilities package.\n"
#| "3. Add back together the results for each partition.\n"
msgid ""
"1. Group the terms of all observables into a partition.  This can be done by using the [`PauliList` API](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.PauliList#group_qubit_wise_commuting), for example.\n"
"     <Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"      You can use the [`BitArray`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.BitArray#expectation_values) primitive attribute to compute the expectation values of the provided observables.\n"
"     </Admonition>\n"
"2. Execute one basis change circuit per partition (whichever basis change needs to be done for each partition). See the Measurement bases addon utility [`measurement_bases` module](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-utils/apidocs/qiskit_addon_utils.exp_vals.html#qiskit_addon_utils.exp_vals.get_measurement_bases) for more information. For more information, see the [documentation](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-utils/) for the Qiskit addon utilities package.\n"
"3. Add back together the results for each partition.\n"
msgstr ""
"1. Grupuhin ang mga term ng lahat ng observable sa isang partition. Maaari itong gawin sa pamamagitan ng paggamit ng [`PauliList` API](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.PauliList#group_qubit_wise_commuting), halimbawa.\n"
"     <Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"      Maaari mong gamitin ang attribute ng primitive na [`BitArray`](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/docs/en/api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.BitArray#expectation_values) para kalkulahin ang mga expectation value ng mga ibinigay na observable.\n"
"     </Admonition>\n"
"2. Ipatupad ang isang basis change circuit bawat partition (anumang pagbabago ng batayan ang kailangang gawin para sa bawat partition). Tingnan ang addon utility ng Measurement bases [`measurement_bases` module](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-utils/apidocs/qiskit_addon_utils.exp_vals.html#qiskit_addon_utils.exp_vals.get_measurement_bases) para sa karagdagang impormasyon. Para sa karagdagang impormasyon, tingnan ang [dokumentasyon](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-utils/) para sa Qiskit addon utilities package.\n"
"3. Idagdag nang magkasama ang mga resulta para sa bawat partition.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Restrictions {#restrictions}"
msgstr "Mga paghihigpit {#restrictions}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Review any [Feature compatibility table](/guides/estimator-options#options-compatibility-table) to understand restrictions when using dynamic circuits. Note that feature compatibility is not primitive-dependent.\n"
msgstr "Suriin ang anumang [Talahanayan ng feature compatibility](/guides/estimator-options#options-compatibility-table) para maunawaan ang mga paghihigpit kapag gumagamit ng mga dynamic na circuit. Tandaan na ang compatibility ng feature ay hindi nakasalalay sa primitive.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr "Mga susunod na hakbang {#next-steps}"

#. type: Plain text
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid ""
